@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #333333
  ArrowColor #333333
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #555555
}
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 45

title SPWPOS - Use Case Overview (system context, 72 use cases in 8 subsystems)
actor "User" as User
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "External AI Service\n<<secondary>>" as AI
actor "Notification Service\n<<secondary>>" as NS
rectangle "SPWPOS System" {
  rectangle "**Account & Profile**\nUC01-UC08 (8 use cases)" as P_ACC #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Task Management**\nUC09-UC26 (18 use cases)" as P_TASK #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Time Management**\nUC27-UC35 (9 use cases)" as P_TIME #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Planning & Scheduling**\nUC36-UC49 (14 use cases)" as P_PLAN #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Execution & Feedback**\nUC50-UC57 (8 use cases)" as P_EXEC #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Intelligence & Personalization**\nUC58-UC64 (7 use cases)" as P_INTEL #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Notification**\nUC65-UC68 (4 use cases)" as P_NOTI #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Administration**\nUC69-UC72 (4 use cases)" as P_ADMIN #FFFFFF
}
User --> P_ACC
User --> P_TASK
User --> P_TIME
User --> P_PLAN
User --> P_EXEC
User --> P_INTEL
User --> P_NOTI
Admin --> P_ADMIN
P_TASK -- AI : UC25, UC26
P_NOTI -- NS : UC65-UC68
P_INTEL ..> P_EXEC : <<include>>\nUC64->UC57
P_NOTI ..> P_INTEL : <<extend>>\nUC67->UC62
P_NOTI ..> P_PLAN : <<extend>>\nUC67->UC44, UC68->UC47
P_PLAN ..> P_EXEC : <<extend>>\nUC45->UC53, UC45->UC54
P_PLAN ..> P_INTEL : <<include>>\nUC36->UC58, UC49->UC61
P_PLAN ..> P_TASK : <<extend>>\nUC45->UC09, UC45->UC12
P_PLAN ..> P_TIME : <<extend>>\nUC45->UC28, UC45->UC32
P_TASK ..> P_INTEL : <<include>>\nUC09->UC58
legend bottom
  Dependency arrows summarise cross-subsystem <<include>> / <<extend>> relationships between individual use cases
  (full detail in the eight subsystem diagrams and the complete diagram).
endlegend
@enduml